"displayValue":"1st"}}],"gameInfo":{"venue":{"id":"4461","fullName":"Princess Auto Stadium","address":{"city":"Winnipeg","country":"Canada"},"grass":false,"images":[]},"attendance":32342,"officials":[{"fullName":"Scott Cherrey","displayName":"Scott Cherrey","position":{"name":"Linesman","displayName":"Linesman","id":"25"},"order":0},{"fullName":"Kyle Rehman","displayName":"Kyle Rehman","position":{"name":"Referee","displayName":"Referee","id":"24"},"order":0},{"fullName":"Furman South","displayName":"Furman South","position":{"name":"Referee","displayName":"Referee","id":"24"},"order":0},{"fullName":"Bevan Mills","displayName":"Bevan Mills","position":{"name":"Linesman","displayName":"Linesman","id":"25"},"order":0}]},"article":{"headline":"Canadiens hold off the Jets 2-1 outdoors in the NHL Heritage Classic","description":"— Jacob Fowler made 33 saves and the Montreal Canadiens held off the Winnipeg Jets 2-1 on Sunday night in the NHL Heritage Classic at Princess Auto Stadium.","story":"WINNIPEG, Manitoba -- — <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5188437/jacob-fowler\">Jacob Fowler</a> made 33 saves and the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/mtl/montreal-canadiens\">Montreal Canadiens</a> held off the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/wpg/winnipeg-jets\">Winnipeg Jets</a> 2-1 on Sunday night in the NHL Heritage Classic at Princess Auto Stadium.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5080230/lane-hutson\">Lane Hutson</a> and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4697399/kaiden-guhle\">Kaiden Guhle</a> scored and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4565236/cole-caufield\">Cole Caufield</a> had two assists to help Montreal improve to 6-3-2. The Canadiens opened a four-game trip Friday night with a 4-1 victory over Chicago. Fowler has won his last five starts.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4874731/isak-rosen\">Isak Rosen</a> scored for Winnipeg with 4:46 remaining at home of the Canadian Football League's Winnipeg Blue Bombers. <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4268767/stuart-skinner\">Stuart Skinner</a> stopped 19 shots for the Jets (4-4-3).\n\n\r\n              The Jets became just the second Canadian team after Edmonton to host two outdoor games. The Jets also were blanked 3-0 by the Oilers in the first one, but spoiled Calgary’s 2019 outdoor game at Mosaic Stadium in Regina, Saskatchewan, with a 2-1 overtime win.\n\n\r\n              It was Winnipeg’s first game since trading franchise goalier <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3020225/connor-hellebuyck\">Connor Hellebuyck</a> to the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/nj/new-jersey-devils\">New Jersey Devils</a> on Friday. <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4697401/dawson-mercer\">Dawson Mercer</a>, who headlined the return from the Devils, had two shots and one blocked shot in 15:22 of ice time.\n\n\r\n              <hl2>Up next</hl2>\r\n              Canadiens: At St. Louis on Tuesday night.\n\n\r\n              Jets: Host Florida on Tuesday night.\n\n\r\n              ------\n\n\r\n              \r\n                <a href=\"https://apnews.com/hub/nhl\">See AP’s full NHL coverage here</a>","published":"2026-10-26T02:34:46Z"}}